Modifications made in Koemachi (as required by section 4(b) of the license). Koemachi keeps the engine of Spoken World (the parts builder, the instant grammar, the
three-tier mind, the film tools, the page) and changes the following:
 - the model is Thinking Machines' Inkling, reached through Tinker's Anthropic-compatible Messages API by a local server (site/serve.js, site/tinker.js); the Gemini provider,
   Gemini transcription, the Claude artifact host, the Vercel deployment files and the whole "Make it real" video workflow (including its example clips) were removed;
 - voice input uses the browser's Web Speech API;
 - the starting town is a new, original one (app/js/koemachi.js, app/generators/), with new engine parts for it: walkable terraces and steps (app/js/floors.js), an animated sea
   (sea.js), a railway timetable and level crossing (railway.js), four seasons (seasons.js);
 - new features: Look & Fix (lookfix.js), kept-example logging (sessions.js), Japanese phrasings (ja.js), "Save as generator" (savegen.js);
 - the tests were adapted (tests/run.js, tests/check_generators.js and new scenarios); the original starting town is kept in tests/fixtures/legacy_town.js only so that the engine
   scenarios written for it still run (copied unchanged from spoken-world's app/js/stage.js).
